    "body": "@Nadya678 points out that the `display` property is also supported, insofar as it can be set to `none`: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/610#issuecomment-364315417\r\n\r\nWrt `<wbr>`, it looks like Webkit/Blink-based browsers override an inherited `white-space: nowrap` and create a line-break opportunity anyway, but Edge/IE/Gecko do not. I want to run this test on Netscape 4 now... see http://fantasai.tripod.com/FHQR/HTML/misc.htm#NOBR which dates from like 2000 or so. More ancient references can be found with https://www.google.com/search?q=netscape+nobr+wbr",
